	"description": [
		"The study of leadership requires a broad understanding of the many critical contemporary issues emerging in today's environment. This course is designed to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of leadership principles, theories, and practices. The course explores various aspects of leadership, from personal development to organizational dynamics, preparing students to become effective leaders in diverse settings. This course combines insights from business strategy, political science, cognitive psychology, and environmental studies. Not open to first year students. Prerequisite: sophomore status or above."
